on itself, and this is the same host as the 0.12 default.\n- **`src/balances.ts`:** a null balance renders as `USDC unavailable` instead of a number.\n- **`src/kyc.ts`:** added the `expired` status, shown as \"Verification expired\".\n- **`src/trust.ts`:** `setTrustline(USDC)` with no options. 0.12 removed `sponsored`, and it sponsors by default when eligible.\n- **`src/ramp.ts`:** `getRampsQuote` is replaced by `getRampRoutes` plus `quoteRamp`. The rate is `amountIn / amountOut` from the best quote, or `null` when there is none.\n\n**Colleague's note:** I applied all of its steps. Two details differ. I took the ARS rail and the asset identifier from `getRampRoutes` instead of hard-coding them, because the package doesn't document an Argentina rail. I also used the bare origin rather than removing `baseUrl`. The note's suggested `?? '0'` fix for null balances was not used.\n\n**Verification:** I checked the behavior with stub clients outside the repo. A null balance shows \"unavailable\", the 10000 ARS / 8 USDC quote gives 1250, and no route gives `null`. Each KYC status maps to its message, and the trustline call takes no options. I did not call the live API, so the testnet key, the ARS route and the quote values are untested.\n\n**Things to check before release**\n- **Sponsorship:** the old code forced sponsorship. Now it follows the app's Pollar dashboard setting. If sponsorship is turned off there, users pay the trustline reserve.\n- **Multichain balances:** 0.12 can return balances for other chains. The app is Stellar-only today, but a Solana native coin would currently be labelled \"XLM\".\n- **`UPGRADE.md`:** I didn't read it because it isn't in the installed package and I had no GitHub access. The changes come from the installed type definitions and the package README.\n\nNothing is committed. `node_modules/` is untracked, and the repo has no `.gitignore`.","ttft_ms":1643,"type":"result","duration_ms":155044,"uuid":"a8d58b48-af11-4f3f-b0c5-f4e4e256b7ff","ttf